course: dictionary
lesson: 5951
title: Reading clues: the mastiff
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A mastiff is a very large, strong dog with a short coat, a big head and loose skin round its face. People kept mastiffs as guard dogs. You may not know this word yet, but the words around it in the castle story give you clues: «the spiky portcullis» (a heavy gate that drops down), «men-at-arms in casquet and corselet of steel» (helmets and armour), and «mastiffs». Gates, armour and guards all point to a guard dog.
explain: Always ask: what would fit here? In the castle, a big guard dog fits. A tiny lap dog would not. Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «Mastiffs» as big guard-dogs works, so your guess is right.
explain: Mastiffs appear in other places too, but the clues stay the same: look at what the dogs are doing and where they are. If a dog is standing guard at a gate, it is probably a strong, watchful dog. When you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: A mastiff is a very large, strong dog with a short coat.
fact: Mastiffs have a big head and loose skin round the face.
fact: «Mastiffs» were kept as guard dogs, at gates, farms and castles.
fact: The English Mastiff is one of the heaviest dog breeds.
fact: A «portcullis» is a heavy gate that drops down to shut a castle entrance.
exercise: What is a mastiff? | A tall tower on a castle wall | A small dog that sits on laps | *A very large, strong guard dog with a short coat | A kind of heavy gate
exercise: In the castle story, which word means a heavy gate that drops down? | pasty | *portcullis | warders | drawbridge
exercise: Based on the castle story, what job did the mastiffs most likely do? | Pull the carts to market | *Guard the castle | Cook the pasties | Herd the sheep
test: Which words in the castle story are clues that the mastiffs were guard dogs? | *portcullis and men-at-arms | ancient and warders | hollow-sounding and drawbridge | pasty and dozing
test: The English Mastiff is one of the heaviest dog breeds. What does heaviest mean? | *Weighing the most | Living the longest | Having the longest tail | Making the loudest noise
exam: Which description best fits a mastiff? | A small, quick dog that likes to chase cats | A fish that lives in deep water | A bird that guards the gate | *A very large, strong dog with a big head and loose skin round its face
